menuconfig MESHTASTIC_MESHBEACON
	bool "Meshtastic mesh beacon (partial vs. the reference; unsupported by default)"
	default n
	help
	  The reference MeshBeacon modules: a zero-hop "here is my mesh, join
	  me" announcement on MESH_BEACON_APP (port 37) -- a short text and/or
	  an offered channel (name + PSK), region and modem preset -- and the
	  listener that caches an offer heard for a client app to act on (never
	  applied automatically). Both halves are off until their flag is set
	  in ModuleConfig.mesh_beacon.flags (LISTEN / BROADCAST). Compiles in
	  the MeshBeacon protobuf.

	  OFF BY DEFAULT, deliberately: this port broadcasts on the RUNNING
	  radio config only (the primary channel, or any channel-table slot a
	  target names), whereas the reference switches the radio around each
	  transmission whose target names another modem preset or region --
	  the feature that gives the beacon its targets at all. Rather than
	  ship a module that accepts a config and then does part of it, the
	  module stays out of a default image and the admin path answers a
	  mesh_beacon write with a NAK, exactly as the reference does for an
	  excluded module. Opt in for a bench that wants the supported subset.
	  The gate for flipping this default: the multi-preset arc delivering a
	  hold/restore radio switch (docs/MULTI-PRESET-OPERATION.md).

if MESHTASTIC_MESHBEACON

config MESHTASTIC_MESHBEACON_START_DELAY_SEC
	int "Delay before the first beacon after boot or a config change"
	default 60
	range 1 3600
	help
	  The reference staggers periodic modules a few tens of seconds after
	  boot. A change to the section re-arms from here, so an app user's
	  edits coalesce into one beacon.

config MESHTASTIC_MESHBEACON_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC
	int "Smallest broadcast interval, in seconds"
	default 3600
	range 60 604800
	help
	  broadcast_interval_secs below this is raised to it, and 0 means this
	  value (reference default_mesh_beacon_min_broadcast_interval_secs, 1 h:
	  a beacon is an invitation, not a heartbeat). The sim suite lowers it
	  to run the cadence in virtual time.

endif # MESHTASTIC_MESHBEACON
